// TEST: T^1 parameter fed a scalar (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
// ERROR-CONTAINS: is an ARRAY by declaration
// ============================================================================
// The caret is a rank CLAIM (see 030): a `T^1` parameter is an array by
// declaration, so a scalar in that position is the wrong shape -- not a
// broadcast. Lifting would have to invent an axis, so the lift declines and
// the conflict is reported.
//
// The escape this closes is the same one the `T^0` cases had, and it reached
// g++ the same way: `T` took argument 1's `Array<double,1>`, argument 2's
// teaching was discarded, and the emitted call handed a bare double to an
// array parameter. Note what makes it invisible to the ordinary rank check --
// a `T^k` parameter is still an OPEN inference variable at the call site
// (that is what keeps HM alive here), so `concreteRankOf` declines it and
// every rank comparison stands down.
// ============================================================================
function rs(a: T^1, b: T^1) -> T^1 = a + b

let A: Array<Float like Idx<3>> = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let s = 5.0

let r = rs(A, s)
